# Satori Enso — agent context

Marketing site for a one-person web studio (Belarus). UI copy is Russian by default and English at `/en/`. Node **>= 22.18**.

## Stack

- Next.js 16 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS 4
- Static export: `output: 'export'`, `trailingSlash: true`
- Content lives in TypeScript modules in the repo. No CMS, no database
- UI copy is `content/messages.ts`: Russian (`/`) and English (`/en/`). See `i18n`
- Images are precompressed (AVIF/WebP) with width and height. The default `next/image` optimizer is off
- Fonts via `next/font` (Cyrillic and Latin subsets), self-hosted at build time
- README, rules, and commit messages are English
- Keep the `magic-string` override. Tailwind's Node bundle `require()`s it; newer magic-string is ESM-only and breaks `next build`

## Local dev

`docker compose up --build` starts project `satori-enso` (its own group in Docker Desktop). The web container runs `next dev --webpack` with polling, because Windows bind mounts do not emit file events. The repo is mounted; `node_modules` and `.next` stay in named volumes (Linux binaries, not the Windows host install). Host port is `WEB_PORT` (default 3010). Do not also run `npm run dev` on the host — that binds 3000, which Nechto already uses.

Install and lockfile edits need Node **22.18**. The default shell may be Node 20. Production is still the static `out/` upload, not this container.

## Hosting

hoster.by Unix shared hosting. Build locally, upload `out/` to the site root. HTTPS redirect is the panel's job.

Do not add a Node server, VPS, or `next start` for production. Static export cannot use Server Actions, request-bound Route Handlers, cookies, or `next.config` redirects.

A lead form, when one is built, is a normal `<form method="post">` to `public/api/lead.php` (`mail()`). Secrets stay above the web root and out of git. Do not put mail or Telegram tokens in client JavaScript.

## Boundaries

- Pages compose sections. Prices and service facts come from content modules
- No secrets in client code
- Format with Prettier. Do not hand-format against it
- Keep changes scoped
